      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "but the construction is ambiguous, गहन being a noun as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "well as an adjective. In the third line the comp. कपालपा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "णिपुटके is to be understood as a Madhyamapadalopî. Then follows",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "भिक्षाटनम्. Now what relation is there between कपाल० and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "भिक्षाटनम् ? If any sense is to be given to the clause we must",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "understand पुटके भिक्षा तदर्थमटनम् taking it as एकदेशी अन्वय.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Perhaps the poet wrote ०पुटकः qualifying रुद्रः, के being a mistake",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "for को committed by some careless scribe. Again in the fourth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "line the causal sense so prominently expressed by नियमित, क्षिप्त",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "and कारित altogether disappears भ्राम्यति being used. Thus there",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "is the fault called प्रक्रमभङ्ग.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 101. आकृतिः—stands for शोभनाकृति a graceful form.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "फलति—bears the desired fruit. संचितानि—Fate is of three",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "kinds; संचित, प्रारब्ध, and क्रियमाण. There is a reference here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to the first kind. The fig. is दीपक the predicate expressing the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "धर्म being only once expressed. There is also उपमा.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 102. महार्णवे—अर्णांसि सन्त्यस्मिन् इति अर्णवः; fr. अर्णस् water",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "+ the matub. aff व, the स् being irregularly dropped before it.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "विषमस्थितम्—in a critical or trying position. विषम is a generic",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "term for difficulty. Cf. Bhatti VI. 88. and Bg. II. 2. where",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the venerable S'ankaráchàrya renders विषमे by सभयस्थाने.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "पुराकृतानि पुण्यानि—This and the preceding sl. show that the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "author believed in a former birth, which Buddism does not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "recognise. See Introduction. Cf. अरक्षितं तिष्ठति दैवरक्षितम् । Pt. 1.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 103. हित—a well-wisher. Cf. हितान्न यः संशृणुते स किंप्रभुः ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Ki. I. 5 प्रत्यक्षम्—अक्ष्णोः प्रति अभिमुखं Avya; अक्षि is changed to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "अक्ष at the end of an Avya. when preceded by प्रति, पर changed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "to परो, सम् and अनु, by प्रतिपरसमनुभ्योऽक्ष्णः । or better अक्षमिन्द्रियं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "प्रतिगतम् Tat, by the Várt. अत्यादयः क्रान्ताद्यर्थे द्वितीयया' । अक्षि when",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "compounded has the general sense of an organ of sense; वृत्तिविषये",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "अक्षिशब्द इन्द्रियमात्रपरः । Manoramá. हालाहलम्—Properly the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "very deadly poison produced at the churning of the ocean; hence",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "any virulent poison. सत्क्रिया—virtuous conduct. Cf. 'शकुन्तला",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
